# etude-ldf platform test partition review

The shared doctor runtime remains cross-platform. POSIX-specific fixtures and
literal quoting oracles now compile and run only on non-Windows platforms;
Windows has a native test file for its parser, argument quoting, case-insensitive
environment, forward-slash explicit paths, indeterminate `env -i`, and
unknown-shell config remediation.

This is a test-only partition. `make test` passes on the host and the Windows CLI
test binary cross-compiles successfully.
